Meta.DisplayName=Space Engineers 2 (SE2 Online) AMP 3
Meta.Description=Space Engineers 2 with the SE2 Online multiplayer plugin, as a headless dedicated server under Wine. The application id, the ports and the launcher are this template's own, so nothing here can move another template. Installation never depends on a folder that already exists: the two signed artefacts published by the plugin author (the 45 MB server build and the 7.4 GB standalone runtime that carries the SE2 engine files and a portable .NET 9) are either downloaded by URL and verified by size and sha256, or taken from an archive the operator drops in the instance's packs folder, recognised by name, size and sha256. The launch binary is not assumed: the install step records the .exe it actually found and the launcher reads that record. Update also bootstraps Windows SteamCMD under Wine, because the runtime ships steam_api64.dll but not the Steam client libraries.
Meta.OS=Linux
Meta.AarchSupport=Unsupported
Meta.Arch=x86_64
Meta.Author=Hellm4n
Meta.URL=https://github.com/Hellm4nbot/amp-templates/blob/main/README.md
Meta.DisplayImageSource=steam:1133870
Meta.EndpointURIFormat=
Meta.ConfigManifest=space-engineers2-se2online-amp3config.json
Meta.MetaConfigManifest=space-engineers2-se2online-amp3metaconfig.json
Meta.ConfigRoot=space-engineers2-se2online-amp3.kvp
Meta.MinAMPVersion=3.0.0.0
Meta.SpecificDockerImage=cubecoders/amp3base:wine-stable
Meta.DockerRequired=False
Meta.DockerBaseReadOnly=False
Meta.ContainerPolicy=RecommendedOnLinux
Meta.ContainerPolicyReason=The SE2 Online dedicated server is a Windows .NET program: it runs under Wine on Linux, and the container carries Wine so the host does not have to.
Meta.ExtraSetupStepsURI=
Meta.Prerequisites=[]
Meta.ExtraContainerPackages=[]
Meta.ConfigReleaseState=NotSpecified
Meta.NoCommercialUsage=False
Meta.ConfigVersion=5
Meta.ReleaseNotes=AMP 3 adaptation of the CubeCoders SE2 Online template. The original failed on "cd: /amp/space-engineers2/: No such file or directory" because its install stage changed into the application folder before creating it; every path here is created first, and no stage depends on a folder that may not exist. Sources are version.php's signed artefacts (URL + sha256) or an operator archive in packs/. The .exe name is discovered, not assumed.
Meta.BreakingReleaseNotes=
Meta.AppConfigId=0217bc1e-519d-4563-a850-5ae2d468e75e
Meta.ImportableExtensions=[]
Meta.AppIsMultiIPAware=False
